# Which release files are built from the Rust port (rust/); every other one
# comes from Go (go/). One asset name per line. Both builds use the same
# file names, config, state and protocols, so nodes switch by their normal
# update, and Go and Rust nodes work together in one mesh.
#
# Possible lines (see PARITY.md for what is verified on each):
#   meshgate-linux-amd64
#   meshgate-linux-arm64
#   meshgate-linux-arm
#   meshgate-freebsd-amd64
#   meshgate-freebsd-arm64
#   meshgate-windows-amd64.zip
#   meshgate-windows-arm64.zip
#
# macOS files (meshgate-darwin-amd64/arm64) are always Rust: Go never had them.
#
# To go back to Go for a file, delete its line: the next release ships Go
# again (a newer version), and nodes update to it as usual.
meshgate-linux-amd64
meshgate-linux-arm64
meshgate-linux-arm
meshgate-freebsd-amd64
meshgate-freebsd-arm64
meshgate-windows-amd64.zip
meshgate-windows-arm64.zip
